. Analizar si los contratos se agrupan por tipo de servicio o suministro.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 73 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 26.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 2.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.0 to 3.6. December accounts for 16% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 9% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 55 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,950 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the presence of multiple awardees do not indicate improper conduct. These patterns could reflect normal market fluctuations or budgetary decisions, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the distribution of contracts by month and awardee to identify unusual patterns. Review contract details for [1] to see if the amount was near the limit due to market rates or budget constraints.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["n91Pfw9DBxWAAM7L03kM8A%3D%3D","WKEXqEpAgcvCfVQHDepjGQ%3D%3D","q5Mt5p%2F5LAo4NavIWzMcHA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}